{"event": "web_search", "client_ms": 14611, "data": {"request_id": "f0b6fd4dab04", "seq": 16, "ts": "2026-10-27T18:11:08.981Z", "t_ms": 14459, "agent": "research", "tool": "tavily_search", "server": "tavily-remote-mcp", "transport": "streamable_http", "purpose": "find current developments on the topic", "query": "Mount Everest summit atmospheric pressure hPa torr kPa", "time_range": null, "status": "ok", "latency_ms": 2596, "results": [{"cite_id": "W5", "url": "https://mountainmedicineblog.7thwave.io/cgi-bin/renderpost.py?postid=1235", "title": "The Pressure Effect", "domain": "mountainmedicineblog.7thwave.io", "score": 0.7829, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-27T18:11:06.384Z", "snippet": "Barometric pressure measurements taken at the South Col (7975m) on Mt Everest between May 22nd 2019 and August 1st 2020. The units on the y axis are hPa which can be converted to KPa by dividing by a factor of 10. Sea level barometric pressure is approximately 101.1KPa [...] The "}, {"cite_id": "W6", "url": "https://hypertextbook.com/facts/2001/JaredGoldberger.shtml", "title": "Pressure on Earth, Lowest - The Physics Factbook", "domain": "hypertextbook.com", "score": 0.7247, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-27T18:11:06.384Z", "snippet": "| Sengupta, Debangsu, Wisselinkm Simon, Chengm Yain. Himalayas- Where the Earth meets the Sky. ThinkQuest. 1997 | \"The atmospheric pressure at the summit of Mt. Everest is about a third that at sea level\" | 33.7 kPa |\n| CRC Press. Handbook of Chemistry and Physics. 61st Ed. 1981."}, {"cite_id": "W7", "url": "https://www.vaia.com/en-us/textbooks/chemistry/chemistry-the-central-science-13-edition/chapter-10/problem-19-the-typical-atmospheric-pressure-on-top-of-mt-eve", "title": "Problem 19 The typical atmospheric pressure... [FREE ... - Vaia", "domain": "www.vaia.com", "score": 0.6957, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-27T18:11:06.384Z", "snippet": "The typical atmospheric pressure on top of Mt. Everest ( 29 , 028 ft ) is about 265 torr. Convert this pressure to (a) atm, (b) mm Hg , (c) pascals, (d) bars, ( ...Read more"}, {"cite_id": "W8", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6863078", "title": "Barometric pressures at extreme altitudes on Mt. Everest", "domain": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "score": 0.6554, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-27T18:11:06.384Z", "snippet": "by JB West · 1983 · Cited by 190 — Data from weather balloons show that the pressure at the altitude of the summit of Mt. Everest varies considerably with season, being about 11.5 Torr higher in ...Read more"}]}}
